rows.en:
I can't stand it anymore.
I have to see someone fall from the roof.
And I want to know whether they survive!{p}

By the time Aizawa got there, a pool of blood had already spread far and wide around Kuwahata, who lay limp and motionless.
He watched him closely for a while, but there was no sign of movement.
When he touched him, the body had already gone cold.{p}

"...He's dead."
Aizawa smiled, satisfied.
Now he knew the result, and the weight on his heart was gone.{p}

But when three delinquents had killed themselves one after another, even the school couldn't keep quiet any longer.
Was a war breaking out between delinquents, or was some other problem at work? The police investigation grew tougher as well.
And as a first step, the roof was put off-limits.{p}

Once he'd called the friend out, he suddenly attacked from behind and made the friend breathe in chloroform.
Just like the first experiment, it worked without a hitch.
But now he had to haul this limp guinea pig all the way to the school roof.{p}

He felt as if he had become the king of this world.
Any of those wretched humans he could see from this spot, he could put an end to their lives any time he pleased.
The thought struck him as hilarious.{p}

Then, when they searched Aizawa's house, they found everything that had happened recorded in detail in his diary.
And, astonishingly, even the events of his final moments the night before, which he couldn't possibly have written.
It was written down as if he had foreseen how things would turn out.{p}

Naturally, neither the police nor the school believed that part.
Someone who threw himself off a roof couldn't possibly write down everything up to the very instant of his death.
The diary ended like this.{p}

Now, everything is still shrouded in mystery.
And that's the end of my story.
Well then, I'll hand things over to the next person.{p}

Does this school hold some kind of secret, I wonder?
...We're getting close to the roof now.
Look, once we climb these stairs, the roof is right there.{p}

"It's Aizawa!
Look, it's Aizawa!"
Arai, who had been gripping the railing beside {f:me|me}, suddenly pointed into the empty air and climbed right over it.{p}

And as he plunged toward the ground... he suddenly vanished{f:.|.}
It was as if his particles had come apart and melted straight into the air; he was gone without a trace{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} slowly looked up at the sky, stunned.{p}

Of course.
That's proof that you're normal, {a}{f:.|.}
Everyone has what they call a defensive instinct, it seems...
But there was once someone who felt no fear at all, no matter how frightening the place.{p}

I see.
That's a serious matter, you know.
Well, I'll talk about that some other time.{p}

This is my chance, Morikawa thought.
He told the teacher he had a stomachache and sat out P.E.
For a while he lay in the nurse's office, but after about ten minutes he slipped out of bed and went back to the classroom.{p}

That's right, he threw it in the trash can.
Then he quietly went back to the nurse's office.
After fourth period ended, he waited a while, then went back to the classroom.{p}

When the teacher came in, the kids sitting around Nakayama whispered to cheer her up.
"Yoko, I'll help you look later."
"You'll find it."{p}

"Today, I'm going to kill something even more fun.
I'll tell you about it next time."
With that, she walked away.{p}

(Something more fun...?
What the hell is she planning to do★)
Morikawa stood frozen on the spot until she was out of sight.{p}

There was another noise.
(Maybe it's the neighbors' TV?)
That was how unreal it was: a violent noise, just like a sound effect.{p}

Just then, a scream suddenly came from inside.
"Mom★"
He flung the door open.{p}

Not long after that, Nakayama started coming to school again.
I heard all this when I went to visit Morikawa in the hospital.
To me, he didn't look like he was lying.
What do you think, {a}{f:?|?}
Do you believe what Morikawa said?{p}

...They say the killer still breaks into people's homes and commits murder.
You should be very careful to lock up at night too, {a}{f:.|.}{p}That's the end of my story.
Next, please.{p}
